     1	"""exp_21 (bf_fa_cartesian) — the EVALUATION side: ``eval_FLAC.py`` + ``eval_pl.py``.
     2	
     3	Rounds 1-2 made ``fa_cartesian`` trainable. ``eval_FLAC.py`` still rejects it, so
     4	the arm cannot be measured; this round makes it a first-class ``cond_method``
     5	there and closes the ``eval_pl.py`` provenance hole the r2 review flagged
     6	(nit 3). The contracts pinned here are plan §3d, §3h item 10 and §5.
     7	
     8	RED first. Before the implementation ``eval_FLAC.evaluate_model`` raises
     9	``Unknown cond_method`` for ``fa_cartesian``, ``orbit_provenance`` returns the
    10	NO-ORBIT pair ``("n/a", None)`` for it, argparse rejects the choice, and
    11	``eval_pl`` has no guard at all.
    12	
    13	**Not every test here is red, and the passing ones are the point of half the
    14	round** (r2 review nit 2 convention — a red-phase description must match the
    15	recorded evidence). Three groups are DELIBERATE NO-CHANGE PINS, marked
    16	``NO-CHANGE PIN`` in their docstrings:
    17	
    18	* the output-filename rule. ``build_output_paths`` already inserts
    19	  ``_<cond_method>_a<n>`` for every non-vanilla method, so ``_fa_cartesian_a4``
    20	  falls out unmodified. The plan says verify, do not fork (§3d); these tests are
    21	  what makes a later fork fail here.
    22	* the ``fa_invariant`` / ``vanilla`` records. Widening an equality test to a
    23	  membership test can silently change the OTHER branch, and every row already in
    24	  ``model_comparison.md`` was written by these two paths. The golden below is a
    25	  literal capture of the pre-change record, key ORDER included.
    26	* the eval chunk plan (§3h item 10). ``fa_cartesian_conditioning`` and the orbit
    27	  executor already implement it; what this round adds is that eval REACHES them,
    28	  so the batch-64/cap-64 vs batch-64/cap-32 split is pinned against the function
    29	  the eval path will call.
    30	
    31	The conditioner fixtures come from ``test_fa_cartesian`` — the sibling module
    32	that owns them (pytest prepends ``src/tests``; same import route as
    33	``test_finetune_cond`` -> ``test_cond_dispatch``). ``test_eval_paths.py`` is NOT
    34	imported and NOT edited: it is exp_03/exp_11/exp_14's audited record of the
    35	vanilla + fa_invariant eval contract and part of this round's regression set, so
    36	leaving it byte-unchanged is what makes its green run evidence that this round
    37	disturbed neither method.
    38	"""
    39	import json
    40	import subprocess
    41	import sys
    42	import types
    43	from pathlib import Path
